## Solutions

- **Find hidden UX issues**: UXCam reveals usability problems that are invisible in QA testing but cause real user frustration. Session replay shows exactly what users experience — a button that doesn't respond, a flow that breaks on specific devices, a screen that confuses first-time users. Teams find and fix critical issues in hours instead of weeks. Recora discovered elderly users were pressing and holding instead of tapping — a 10-minute fix reduced support tickets by 142%.
- **Optimize conversion funnels**: UXCam Funnel Analytics identifies the exact step where users drop off in registration, checkout, onboarding, and upgrade flows. Product intelligence explains why users leave at each step, backed by session replay evidence. Costa Coffee found that 15% of users abandoned registration after invalid password errors — simplifying the flow increased registrations by 15%.
- **Drive feature adoption**: UXCam shows why users ignore features that teams spent months building. Product analytics measures adoption rates, and session replay reveals what blocks usage — confusing UI, buried entry points, or broken flows on specific devices. Housing.com watched 50-100 sessions daily and redesigned their multi-area search, growing adoption from 20% to 40%.
- **Reduce support tickets**: UXCam replaces vague user reports with visual evidence of what actually happened. Instead of guessing what "it's not working" means, teams watch the session, see the problem, and fix it. Product intelligence surfaces the issues generating the most support volume so teams prioritize the highest-impact fixes.
- **Improve retention**: UXCam tracks retention cohorts and surfaces why users churn after day 1, 7, or 30. AI-powered product analytics identifies frustration patterns — rage taps, repeated errors, crash loops — that predict churn before it happens. Inspire Fitness used UXCam to boost time-in-app by 460% and reduce rage taps by 56%.
- **Validate changes fast**: UXCam lets teams verify whether a fix actually worked in real usage — not just in staging. Heatmaps and session replays show immediate behavioral impact after a release, replacing weeks of waiting for statistical significance. PlaceMakers found a problem, tested a fix, and validated the result in 3 days.

